# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# Newton and dogleg Hessians are analytic and are not force calls.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied: the problem file has no energy_tol, rmsd_tol, or per-start reference.
# energy_min and energy_max are the final potential values on the recorded points.
# Default row. gtol and the iteration budget are the problem force norm and the force-call cap. This row fixes L-BFGS memory at 20. The shipped L-BFGS memory is 10. maxstep is 0.2, the per-atom displacement cap (rgmin atom_maxmove, the same quantity as the eOn max move and the rgmin ASE default). istep is 0.1. BB, DIIS, FIRE, and quickmin take that gradient trial with no line search. L-BFGS, BFGS, CG, steepest descent, Adam, SR1, and SR2 use the session strong Wolfe search, and the first trial is still sized by istep. Newton and dogleg take a Hessian step inside the same cap. Without the cap, an uncapped gradient trial on these starts leaves the Lennard-Jones cutoff. The same values are used for every start.
